@LiNiMGI 
We will create holdase chaperone activity https://github.com/geneontology/go-ontology/issues/30552

Once this is available, you can annotate TIM10 and TIM12.

Good question. I  think that "holdases" always "deliver"  the unfolded protein  to another protein (i.e. a foldase), or to an insertase (as in the case of the Tiny Tims).

It depends on what we class as a "cellular component" in this situation.  If this is a GO "cellular component", it  doesn't really fit correctly.  We should probably concentrate on the "entity" it delivers to rather than the "cellular component"

